{"id": "EUVD-2026-59304", "enisaUuid": "fa4195fb-a954-3594-8f22-5a42eccb0d01", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: udp_tunnel: prevent double queueing in udp_tunnel_nic_device_sync\n\nYue Sun reported a use-after-free and debugobjects warning in\nudp_tunnel_nic_device_sync_work() during concurrent device operations.\n\nThe workqueue core clears the internal pending bit before invoking the\nworker. At that point, a concurrent thread can queue the work again.\nWhen the already running worker eventually clears the work_pending flag\nto 0, it mistakenly clears the flag for the newly queued instance.\nudp_tunnel_nic_unregister() then observes work_pending as 0 and frees\nthe structure while the second work item is still active in the queue,\nleading to UAF.\n\nFix this by returning early in udp_tunnel_nic_device_sync() if\nwork_pending is already set, preventing redundant work queueing.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:56:29", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:44:51", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f49ed02fd8c98da823fdd7b00d64a8cc1d1883ac", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cee6688e5731c0591643521716d1a1a5c1a98bf8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9075efb9b2c1d9d7a8285c937b64aa93ca0c41b7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/54292b167466cdf42176b7b6f01da66c184deb12", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ecf69d4b43370c587e48d4d70289dbdb7e039d4d"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-72405", "GHSA-w888-j23q-c78g"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1185fe52-af21-31c2-b878-c26d03d2d545", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cc4e3835eff474aa274d6e1d18f69d9d296d3b76 <f49ed02fd8c98da823fdd7b00d64a8cc1d1883ac"}, {"id": "3443b09a-ea30-302c-8128-693d51c8cc94", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "3e41b9b4-2f86-3fc6-be79-a2535db3b245", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.40"}, {"id": "46c9c19a-20b5-3647-8f84-87ae059987fb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "6eb860db-7a53-3320-9c5e-48e2769e00c5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.9"}, {"id": "725cbc1a-e9c7-3e45-9ac4-3c96de720d0e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "8e293b97-cf5a-386c-8004-bd4ac36fd5e5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cc4e3835eff474aa274d6e1d18f69d9d296d3b76 <cee6688e5731c0591643521716d1a1a5c1a98bf8"}, {"id": "aa460728-bb2b-35c2-8d59-c70460b4d447", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cc4e3835eff474aa274d6e1d18f69d9d296d3b76 <54292b167466cdf42176b7b6f01da66c184deb12"}, {"id": "acb35026-d785-30b6-b2e3-378f522d3e1f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.97"}, {"id": "ccbf6d4d-eb53-3081-a696-f306996f44c0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cc4e3835eff474aa274d6e1d18f69d9d296d3b76 <ecf69d4b43370c587e48d4d70289dbdb7e039d4d"}, {"id": "d04b4f66-dadf-3bca-9489-2c727d4d166b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cc4e3835eff474aa274d6e1d18f69d9d296d3b76 <9075efb9b2c1d9d7a8285c937b64aa93ca0c41b7"}, {"id": "e5f8060c-a6d7-3100-a5d5-7d76d612568a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "2ed9ab28-273e-3daa-83f1-8c4ad80878a3", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}